  (169, 19, 3, 'Any time. If you need more, open a billing ticket so it is tracked.', FALSE, '2026-06-26 12:41:00'),
  (170, 1, 15, 'Made the Caprese with tomatoes from my neighbour. Never going back to supermarket ones.', FALSE, '2026-06-28 09:10:00'),
  (171, 1, 6, 'Ripe tomatoes and good oil, that is the whole recipe.', FALSE, '2026-06-28 09:30:00'),
  (172, 20, 6, 'Welcome to the Italian Kitchen! A room for pasta, pizza, risotto and strong opinions.', FALSE, '2026-07-14 18:03:00'),
  (173, 20, 9, 'Merci Marco! Can I bring Provencal cousins? Pissaladiere counts, right?', FALSE, '2026-07-14 18:15:00'),
  (174, 20, 6, 'It is basically pizza''s French cousin, so yes.', FALSE, '2026-07-14 18:21:00'),
  (175, 20, 12, 'I made your carbonara twice already. The first time the eggs scrambled.', FALSE, '2026-07-14 19:51:00'),
  (176, 20, 6, 'Classic. Take the pan off the heat before adding the egg mixture, and keep a splash of pasta water.', FALSE, '2026-07-14 20:06:00'),
  (177, 20, 12, 'Second attempt was silky. Thank you!', FALSE, '2026-07-14 20:26:00'),
  (178, 20, 11, 'Is there a good vegetarian alternative to guanciale? Mushrooms?', FALSE, '2026-07-15 00:26:00'),
  (179, 20, 6, 'Smoked mushrooms or toasted breadcrumbs for the crunch. Not authentic, but tasty.', FALSE, '2026-07-15 00:56:00'),
  (180, 20, 15, 'Can a total beginner make fresh pasta?', FALSE, '2026-07-15 10:56:00'),
  (181, 20, 6, 'Absolutely. Flour, eggs, a pinch of salt and patience. Start with tagliatelle, it is forgiving.', FALSE, '2026-07-15 11:21:00'),
  (182, 20, 9, 'And a rolling pin is enough, no machine needed.', FALSE, '2026-07-15 11:31:00'),
  (183, 20, 15, 'Saturday project then!', FALSE, '2026-07-15 11:43:00'),
  (184, 20, 12, 'Report back with photos please.', FALSE, '2026-07-15 11:51:00'),
