  (252, 28, 3, 'You are billed monthly (R30.00) on the day you subscribed. You can cancel from your profile at any time and keep access until the end of the paid period.', FALSE, '2026-08-25 13:27:00'),
  (253, 28, 15, 'That is clear, thanks. And if a payment fails?', FALSE, '2026-08-25 13:43:00'),
  (254, 29, 10, 'Welcome to the Beginner Bakers Help Desk! No question is too small, and burnt bottoms are normal.', FALSE, '2026-08-25 17:03:00'),
  (255, 29, 15, 'Why does my crumble topping go soggy?', FALSE, '2026-08-25 17:38:00'),
  (256, 29, 10, 'Cold butter, rub it in quickly, and do not pack the topping down. Bake until golden, not pale.', FALSE, '2026-08-25 17:52:00'),
  (257, 29, 5, 'A little ground almond in the topping absorbs moisture too.', FALSE, '2026-08-25 18:14:00'),
  (258, 29, 12, 'My oven runs hot, how do I know?', FALSE, '2026-08-25 21:14:00'),
  (259, 29, 10, 'Buy a cheap oven thermometer. It will change your baking.', FALSE, '2026-08-25 21:23:00'),
  (260, 29, 16, 'Ordered one, mine is probably off by 20 degrees.', FALSE, '2026-08-25 22:03:00'),
  (261, 28, 3, 'The subscription goes to past due and we retry. You will see a notice on your profile.', FALSE, '2026-08-26 16:32:00'),
  (262, 29, 15, 'My banana bread did not sink this time, thanks to Julie!', FALSE, '2026-08-26 22:03:00'),
  (263, 29, 10, 'Proud of you Zoe!', FALSE, '2026-08-26 22:09:00'),
  (264, 29, 5, 'Next challenge: a proper puff pastry. I will film it.', FALSE, '2026-08-27 00:09:00'),
  (265, 29, 15, 'Please do, I will unlock it right away.', FALSE, '2026-08-27 00:20:00'),
  (266, 29, 12, 'Same here.', FALSE, '2026-08-27 00:23:00'),
  (267, 28, 15, 'Perfect, thank you for the quick answer.', FALSE, '2026-08-27 18:18:00'),
  (268, 28, 3, 'Any time. If you need more, open a billing ticket so it is tracked.', FALSE, '2026-08-27 18:24:00'),
  (269, 30, 8, 'Welcome to Weeknight Dinners! Rule: under 30 minutes of cooking and as few pans as possible.', FALSE, '2026-09-05 18:33:00'),
  (270, 30, 12, 'My go-to is the omelette with a green salad.', FALSE, '2026-09-05 18:58:00'),
  (271, 30, 8, 'A classic. Add herbs and you are fancy.', FALSE, '2026-09-05 19:07:00'),
  (272, 30, 16, 'Pasta with whatever is in the fridge for me.', FALSE, '2026-09-05 19:57:00'),
  (273, 30, 11, 'Stir-fry is my fridge-clearing champion.', FALSE, '2026-09-05 20:09:00'),
  (274, 30, 15, 'I need ideas that do not fail. Beginner here.', FALSE, '2026-09-06 01:09:00'),
  (275, 30, 8, 'Tuna mayo sandwich, French toast for dinner, burger in a pan. All hard to ruin.', FALSE, '2026-09-06 01:29:00'),
  (276, 30, 4, 'Moderator note: this room is ad-free, share recipes and tips freely.', FALSE, '2026-09-06 11:29:00'),
  (277, 30, 12, 'Noted! Sharing my 15-minute shrimp tonight.', FALSE, '2026-09-06 11:54:00'),
  (278, 30, 16, 'Garlic butter shrimp? Yes please.', FALSE, '2026-09-06 11:59:00'),
  (279, 30, 15, 'Making the French toast tomorrow, wish me luck.', FALSE, '2026-09-06 12:59:00'),
  (280, 1, 12, 'The fresh guacamole recipe is great, thank you Nina!', FALSE, '2026-09-14 08:05:00'),
  (281, 1, 11, 'Thank you Sophie! Ripe avocados only.', FALSE, '2026-09-14 08:30:00'),
  (282, 31, 15, 'Hi Cyp, quick question about the guidelines. Can I put a link to my own blog in my profile?', FALSE, '2026-09-14 08:59:00'),
  (283, 31, 2, 'Hi Zoe! Yes, a link in your profile website field is fine.', FALSE, '2026-09-14 09:05:00'),
  (284, 31, 15, 'And in the lounge chat?', FALSE, '2026-09-14 09:23:00'),
  (285, 31, 2, 'Not as promotion, no. Sharing a recipe you made is welcome, repeated ads are not.', FALSE, '2026-09-14 11:44:00'),
  (286, 31, 15, 'Understood, thanks for clarifying.', FALSE, '2026-09-14 12:04:00'),
  (287, 31, 2, 'Anytime. Enjoy the community!', FALSE, '2026-09-14 12:29:00'),
  (288, 32, 16, 'Marco, I am hosting dinner for six next week and want to serve your Spaghetti Bolognese as the main.', FALSE, '2026-09-24 13:00:00'),
  (289, 32, 6, 'Lovely! What are you thinking for the starter and dessert?', FALSE, '2026-09-24 13:08:00'),
  (290, 32, 16, 'No idea yet. Something light before, and something simple after.', FALSE, '2026-09-24 13:30:00'),
  (291, 32, 6, 'Keep the starter fresh and cold so your oven stays free, and a make-ahead dessert so you can sit with your guests.', FALSE, '2026-09-24 16:50:00'),
  (292, 32, 16, 'That is exactly the kind of advice I needed.', FALSE, '2026-09-24 16:57:00'),
  (293, 32, 6, 'And do one test run if you have never made the main for six.', FALSE, '2026-09-24 22:14:00'),
  (294, 32, 16, 'Good call. I will cook it on Sunday first.', FALSE, '2026-09-24 22:26:00'),
  (295, 33, 7, 'Hey Nina, what are you cooking this weekend?', FALSE, '2026-09-25 14:10:00'),
  (296, 33, 11, 'Hey Awa! Something simple and slow, I think. You?', FALSE, '2026-09-25 14:12:00'),
  (297, 33, 7, 'Probably something quick, I have a busy week. Maybe your Fresh Guacamole again.', FALSE, '2026-09-25 16:52:00'),
  (298, 33, 11, 'Ha, that is a compliment. It is quick enough for a weeknight.', FALSE, '2026-09-25 17:03:00'),
  (299, 33, 7, 'That is why I love it. Send me your next idea when you have one!', FALSE, '2026-09-25 17:30:00'),
  (300, 33, 11, 'Will do. Have a great weekend!', FALSE, '2026-09-25 17:41:00'),
  (301, 1, 2, 'Friendly reminder: the report button is for real guideline issues, please keep it for those.', FALSE, '2026-10-02 10:00:00'),
  (302, 34, 15, 'Hi Lucas, I love your recipes. Would you take a paid request for something custom?', FALSE, '2026-10-04 12:11:00'),
  (303, 34, 5, 'Hi Zoe! Depends on the dish. What do you have in mind?', FALSE, '2026-10-04 12:20:00'),
  (304, 34, 15, 'A dish in the spirit of your Traditional Tarte Tatin, but easier for weeknights, with a short video if possible.', FALSE, '2026-10-04 12:45:00'),
  (305, 34, 5, 'That I can do. Any dietary restrictions I should know about?', FALSE, '2026-10-04 16:14:00'),
  (306, 34, 15, 'No allergies, but I would like less than 30 minutes of active cooking.', FALSE, '2026-10-04 16:31:00'),
  (307, 34, 5, 'Done. Send it through the request form with your budget and I will accept it this week.', FALSE, '2026-10-04 16:35:00'),
  (308, 34, 15, 'Just sent it. Thank you so much!', FALSE, '2026-10-04 16:52:00'),
  (309, 34, 5, 'Received. I will start testing this weekend.', FALSE, '2026-10-04 18:05:00'),
  (310, 35, 16, 'Hi Lucas, can I ask a beginner question? I tried Lemon Garlic Roast Potatoes and it did not look like the photo.', FALSE, '2026-10-12 21:22:00'),
  (311, 35, 5, 'Of course Mpho! What went wrong?', FALSE, '2026-10-12 21:37:00'),
  (312, 35, 16, 'The texture was off and I think I rushed a step.', FALSE, '2026-10-12 21:58:00'),
  (313, 35, 5, 'Rushing or too high heat is the usual culprit for beginners. Lower the heat and give it time.', FALSE, '2026-10-12 23:23:00'),
  (314, 35, 16, 'I will try again slowly. Is it normal to feel nervous in the kitchen?', FALSE, '2026-10-12 23:30:00'),
  (315, 35, 5, 'Totally. Everyone burns something. Read the whole recipe once before starting and prep everything first.', FALSE, '2026-10-12 23:44:00'),
  (316, 35, 16, 'That is a great habit, I always start cooking while still reading.', FALSE, '2026-10-14 07:38:00'),
  (317, 35, 5, 'Try it my way next time and tell me what changed.', FALSE, '2026-10-14 11:02:00'),
  (318, 35, 16, 'Deal. Thank you for being so kind Lucas.', FALSE, '2026-10-14 11:29:00'),
  (319, 1, 15, 'Cinnamon French toast for breakfast. Thank you Julie!', FALSE, '2026-10-19 08:00:00'),
  (320, 36, 11, 'Quick question about your Margherita Pizza, if you have a minute.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 14:35:00'),
  (321, 36, 6, 'Sure Nina, go ahead.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 14:37:00'),
  (322, 36, 11, 'Is it okay to prepare part of it the day before? I am cooking for guests on Saturday.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 18:06:00'),
  (323, 37, 15, 'Hi Marco, can I ask a beginner question? I tried Caprese Salad and it did not look like the photo.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 19:45:00'),
  (324, 37, 6, 'Of course Zoe! What went wrong?', FALSE, '2026-10-26 19:46:00'),
  (325, 37, 15, 'The texture was off and I think I rushed a step.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 19:57:00'),
  (326, 37, 6, 'Rushing or too high heat is the usual culprit for beginners. Lower the heat and give it time.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 20:22:00'),
  (327, 38, 7, 'Tom, could you read my draft for Smoky Braai Yassa? I am not sure the steps are clear.', FALSE, '2026-10-26 21:26:00'),
  (328, 37, 15, 'I will try again slowly. Is it normal to feel nervous in the kitchen?', FALSE, '2026-10-26 21:41:00'),
  (329, 38, 8, 'Sure. Send it over.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 07:24:00'),
  (330, 37, 6, 'Totally. Everyone burns something. Read the whole recipe once before starting and prep everything first.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 07:46:00'),
  (331, 37, 15, 'That is a great habit, I always start cooking while still reading.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 07:57:00'),
  (332, 37, 6, 'Try it my way next time and tell me what changed.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 07:59:00'),
  (333, 37, 15, 'Deal. Thank you for being so kind Marco.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 09:09:00'),
  (334, 38, 7, 'Done, it is in my creations, private for now.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 12:03:00'),
  (335, 38, 8, 'Read it. The steps are good, but split the long step in two and give a visual cue, colour or texture, instead of only a time.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 12:20:00'),
  (336, 36, 6, 'Yes. Do the prep ahead (chopping, sauces, marinades) and keep the final cooking step for the last hour.', FALSE, '2026-10-27 18:34:00'),
  (337, 36, 11, 'Perfect, that takes a lot of stress off. Anything I should avoid doing in advance?', FALSE, '2026-10-27 19:00:00'),
  (338, 39, 13, 'Hi Lucas! I unlocked your video for Traditional Tarte Tatin, it is so much clearer than text.', FALSE, '2026-10-28 10:35:00'),
  (339, 39, 5, 'Thank you Thando! I film the tricky steps in full because they are easier to see.', FALSE, '2026-10-28 11:03:00'),
  (340, 38, 7, 'Good point, cues are more reliable than minutes.', FALSE, '2026-10-28 14:51:00'),
  (341, 38, 8, 'Also add the serving size, people always ask.', FALSE, '2026-10-28 15:02:00'),
  (342, 38, 7, 'Fixing both now. Thank you!', FALSE, '2026-10-28 15:05:00'),
  (343, 36, 6, 'Do not season everything early, salt at the end. And take things out of the fridge a bit before cooking.', FALSE, '2026-10-28 21:28:00'),
  (344, 40, 7, 'Hi Pierre, I had an idea. What if we each cook a version of Hearty Lentil Soup and compare notes in the lounge?', FALSE, '2026-10-29 09:05:00'),
